# pass-edge → Amazon Location Service (Places): build summary

## The constraint (answers "can I bind 2 roles to one SA?")
**No.** Under EKS Pod Identity a service account maps to *exactly one* IAM role in
the cluster account — to change it you edit the association, you don't add a second.
So `pass-edge-sa` can't hold the shared global secrets role **and** a separate geo
role at the same time. (The only "two role" case is cross-account role chaining —
source + target role — which isn't our situation; Location and the cluster are same-account.)

## Design decision
`pass-edge-sa` is currently bound to the shared global secrets role. Two ways to add
geo, one good:

- ❌ **Add geo to the global role** → every app on that role gets Location access.
  Over-permissioned, breaks least privilege.
- ✅ **Dedicated role for pass-edge** = (pass-edge's secrets, scoped) + (the two geo
  actions), then **repoint `pass-edge-sa`** from the global role to this dedicated role.

> Alternative if we're forced to keep a single global role: gate the geo statement with
> ABAC on the pod-identity session tag for `pass-edge-sa`. Works, but bloats the shared
> role with per-app conditions — not recommended.

## What to build
- [x] `pass-edge-role` with the Pod Identity trust policy (`pods.eks.amazonaws.com`,
      `sts:AssumeRole` + `sts:TagSession`) — in `pass-edge-iam-role.tf`.
- [x] Permissions policy: `geo-places:Geocode` + `geo-places:ReverseGeocode` on
      `arn:aws:geo-places:us-east-2::provider/default`.
- [ ] **Secrets scope (deferred):** add `secretsmanager:GetSecretValue` + `kms:Decrypt`,
      scoped to pass-edge's secret ARN(s) and the secrets CMK. Stubs are in the .tf file.
- [ ] **Repoint the association:** change `pass-edge-sa`'s `role_arn` from the global
      secrets role → `pass-edge-role` (the entry in your dev.tfvars pod-identity map).
      This is an *edit* of an existing association, not a fresh create.

## Open items / dependencies
- **Namespace** — Jeff guessed "pass"; confirm the real namespace before repointing the
  association. It has to match exactly or it silently won't attach.
- **Secret ARNs + CMK** — needed to scope the secrets half of the dedicated role. Pull
  from pass-edge's SecretProviderClass.
- **Sequencing (config-before-code):** the dedicated role must carry the secrets access
  **and** the association must be repointed *before* Jeff flips `serviceAccountName` to
  `pass-edge-sa`. Otherwise pass-edge boots under a role with no secrets access.
- **Egress (Jeff's lane):** the pod still has to reach `places.geo.us-east-2.amazonaws.com`
  — either a firewall allowlist entry through Aviatrix or a Location Service VPC endpoint
  (PrivateLink, supported since early 2025). Correct IAM ≠ reachable endpoint.
- **App side (Jeff, confirmed):** pass-edge code already uses the default credential chain
  / pod identity — no rebuild. Just drop the local API-key/referer workaround and make sure
  the SDK region is us-east-2.

## Ownership
- **You (DevOps):** dedicated role + permissions policy + association repoint (Terraform).
- **Jeff:** deployment SA switch; firewall allowlist / VPC endpoint for egress.

## Validate
- `terraform plan` / `apply` in dev.
- `aws iam get-role --role-name pass-edge-role` and
  `aws iam list-attached-role-policies --role-name pass-edge-role` to confirm the role/policy.
- After repoint + deploy: `aws eks list-pod-identity-associations --cluster-name <cluster>`
  should show `pass-edge-sa → pass-edge-role`; then a Geocode call from the pod (once egress
  is open) is the end-to-end check.
